  Remaining NumPy fallbacks (in BEHAVIORAL, shared by TRANSACTIONAL):

  Only for elementwise ops with broadcasting (when tensor shapes don't match):
  - add, sub, mul, div fall back to NumPy when broadcasting is needed
  - This is a known limitation - C++ fabric doesn't support broadcasting yet

  These fallbacks are in execute_op_behavioral at lines 686, 720, 754, 788 and only trigger when a_buf.size != b_buf.size. For equal-size tensors, C++ is used.

  Conclusion: Core compute ops (matmul, linear, conv2d, activations) all use C++. The only NumPy fallback is for broadcasting in elementwise ops, which is a reasonable limitation.

