  Should I investigate why the benchmark efficiency is only 49% instead of the 80% target?

  Root Cause Analysis: Efficiency Gap

  Summary

  The benchmarks are using proper C++ KPU simulation (ConcurrentExecutor with ISA-level modeling). The 49% efficiency is a reporting artifact due to a clock domain mismatch in the configuration.

  Finding: Clock Domain Mismatch
  ┌────────────────────────────────┬────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────────┐
  │           Parameter            │     Value      │                  Source                  │
  ├────────────────────────────────┼────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ HardwareSpec::peak_gflops      │ 1024           │ "16x16 @ 2GHz, 2 ops/cycle"              │
  ├────────────────────────────────┼────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ ConcurrentExecutor cycle model │ 256 FMAs/cycle │ One systolic operation per counted cycle │
  └────────────────────────────────┴────────────────┴──────────────────────────────────────────┘
  The issue: The benchmark calculates GFLOPS as FLOPs / cycles, which implicitly assumes 1 GHz. At 1 GHz, 256 FMAs/cycle = 512 GFLOPS peak (not 1024).

  Verification

  For 1024×1024×1024 matmul:
  ┌───────────────────────────────┬───────────────┬───────────────────────────────────┐
  │            Metric             │     Value     │            Calculation            │
  ├───────────────────────────────┼───────────────┼───────────────────────────────────┤
  │ Total FMAs                    │ 1,073,741,824 │ 1024³                             │
  ├───────────────────────────────┼───────────────┼───────────────────────────────────┤
  │ Ideal compute cycles          │ 4,194,304     │ FMAs / 256                        │
  ├───────────────────────────────┼───────────────┼───────────────────────────────────┤
  │ Actual cycles                 │ 4,370,048     │ (includes data movement overhead) │
  ├───────────────────────────────┼───────────────┼───────────────────────────────────┤
  │ Achieved GFLOPS               │ 491.41        │ 2×FMAs / cycles                   │
  ├───────────────────────────────┼───────────────┼───────────────────────────────────┤
  │ Reported efficiency           │ 48.0%         │ 491.41 / 1024                     │
  ├───────────────────────────────┼───────────────┼───────────────────────────────────┤
  │ Compute utilization           │ 96.0%         │ From executor                     │
  ├───────────────────────────────┼───────────────┼───────────────────────────────────┤
  │ True efficiency (vs 512 peak) │ 96.0%         │ 491.41 / 512                      │
  └───────────────────────────────┴───────────────┴───────────────────────────────────┘
  The compute fabric is actually running at 96% of its modeled throughput. The efficiency reporting is wrong because it uses 1024 GFLOPS peak (2 GHz assumption) when the cycle model operates at 1 GHz equivalent.

  Architecture Confirmation

  The C++ benchmark infrastructure is correct and uses:

  ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
  │                    Benchmark Harness                        │
  │  (src/tools/benchmark/benchmark.cpp)                        │
  └──────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────┘
                         │ Compiles kernel → DMProgram
                         ▼
  ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
  │                  ConcurrentExecutor                         │
  │  (src/software/isa/concurrent_executor.cpp)                 │
  │                                                             │
  │   ┌─────────┐ ┌─────────┐ ┌─────────┐ ┌─────────────────┐   │
  │   │DMA[0-3] │ │BM[0-3]  │ │STR[0-3] │ │Compute Fabric   │   │
  │   │16 GB/s  │ │32 GB/s  │ │32 GB/s  │ │256 FMAs/cycle   │   │
  │   │per ch   │ │per mover│ │per str  │ │(16×16 systolic) │   │
  │   └─────────┘ └─────────┘ └─────────┘ └─────────────────┘   │
  └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

  Options to Fix

  1. Fix HardwareSpec (simple): Change peak_gflops = 512 to match 1 GHz cycle model
  2. Fix cycle model (complex): Scale compute cycles by clock ratio (2000/1000)
  3. Document as-is: Acknowledge efficiency is vs 2 GHz peak, utilization shows true efficiency

  Recommendation

  Option 1 is cleanest: The cycle model counts one 256-FMA operation per cycle. At 1 GHz reference, that's 512 GFLOPS peak. The HardwareSpec::peak_gflops should be 512.

  This would change reported efficiency from 49% to 96%, matching compute utilization.

  Should I make this fix?


