● Here's a summary of the available tools for benchmarking and plotting:

  ---
  Benchmark/Roofline Tools

  1. CLI Tool (kpu-benchmark)

  # Quick sweep (64 to 1024)
  ./build/tools/benchmark/kpu-benchmark sweep --quick -f json -o results.json

  # Roofline analysis
  ./build/tools/benchmark/kpu-benchmark roofline --quick -f json

  # Single benchmark
  ./build/tools/benchmark/kpu-benchmark single -m 512 -n 512 -k 512 -f json

  # All benchmarks
  ./build/tools/benchmark/kpu-benchmark all -f table

  2. Python Roofline Tool (tools/roofline/roofline_plot.py)

  # Demo with sample data (text summary)
  python3 tools/roofline/roofline_plot.py --demo --summary

  # Generate plot from benchmark results (requires matplotlib)
  python3 tools/roofline/roofline_plot.py results.json -o roofline.png

  # Run benchmarks and plot
  python3 tools/roofline/roofline_plot.py --run-benchmark -o roofline.png

  # JSON export
  python3 tools/roofline/roofline_plot.py --demo --json

  3. Combined Workflow

  # Run benchmark, save to JSON, then generate plot
  ./build/tools/benchmark/kpu-benchmark roofline -f json -o roofline_data.json
  python3 tools/roofline/roofline_plot.py roofline_data.json -o roofline.png

  ---
  Note: Plotting requires matplotlib and numpy. To install:
  pip install matplotlib numpy

  The CLI outputs JSON in the format the Python tool expects, so they work together seamlessly.



